# Process Intelligence Telemetry Documentation

Generated version: `{{ schema_version }}`
OpenTelemetry Schema URL: `{{ schema_url }}`

This document defines the process intelligence telemetry framework, strictly honoring the nominal category separations.

## 1. Telemetry Feedstock (Ingestion)
Telemetry is feedstock—raw operational data collected directly from witnesses. It does not carry semantic judgment.

| Attribute Key | Type | Description | Example |
|---|---|---|---|
| `pi.feedstock.witness.id` | string | Unique process witness ID | `wit_sys_exec_01` |
| `pi.feedstock.source` | string | Feedstock telemetry source mechanism | `ebpf_syscall` |
| `pi.feedstock.payload_size` | int | Byte length of the witness report payload | `2048` |

## 2. Process Consequence (Court)
Process consequence is court—the analytical/governance outcome or judicial decision rendered after verifying telemetry feedstock.

| Attribute Key | Type | Description | Example |
|---|---|---|---|
| `pi.court.case.id` | string | Active audit/compliance case identifier | `case_2026_q2_09` |
| `pi.court.verdict.type` | string | Verdict type assigned to the consequence | `violation_halt` |
| `pi.court.verdict.severity` | string | Verdict consequence severity | `critical` |

## 3. Schema Diffs vs Process Drift
- **Weaver Diffs**: Represent structural changes, extensions, or deletions within the semantic convention schema versions.
- **Process Drift**: Represents operational deviations of runtime execution patterns from defined gold-standard models.
Weaver diffs are **not** process drift.

| Attribute Key | Type | Description | Example |
|---|---|---|---|
| `pi.weaver.diff.source_version` | string | Base schema version | `1.0.0` |
| `pi.weaver.diff.target_version` | string | Updated schema version | `1.1.0` |
| `pi.weaver.diff.type` | string | Characterization of the schema diff | `schema_addition` |
